---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const sources = [
  ['United Nations. “Goal 7: Ensure access to affordable, reliable, sustainable and modern energy for all.”', 'https://sdgs.un.org/goals/goal7'],
  ['Georgia Tech Office of Sustainability. “Sustainability Next Plan.”', 'https://sustain.gatech.edu/sustainability-next-plan/'],
  ['Georgia Tech. “Climate Action Plan Provides Road Map to Net-Zero Emissions.” April 5, 2024.', 'https://sustain.gatech.edu/2024/04/05/climate-action-plan-provides-road-map-to-net-zero-emissions/'],
  ['Georgia Tech. “Annual Utility Report, FY2025.” February 2026.', 'https://sustain.gatech.edu/files/2026/02/Georgia-Tech-2025-Annual-Utility-Report-Final-1.pdf'],
  ['Georgia Tech Office of Sustainability. “2025 Sustainability Report.” February 2026.', 'https://sustain.gatech.edu/files/2026/02/2025-Sustainability-Report_2.2026_SPREADS.pdf'],
  ['Georgia Tech Office of Sustainability. “Emissions.”', 'https://sustain.gatech.edu/impact-area-emissions/'],
  ['U.S. Energy Information Administration. “Net Generation by State by Type of Producer by Energy Source, 1990–2024.”', 'https://www.eia.gov/electricity/data/state/'],
  ['U.S. Energy Information Administration. “Plant Vogtle Unit 4 begins commercial operation.” May 1, 2024.', 'https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=61963'],
  ['Georgia Tech. “Students Take the Lead in Campus Energy Decisions Through Hands-On VIP Course.” February 27, 2026.', 'https://www.gatech.edu/news/2026/02/27/students-take-lead-campus-energy-decisions-through-hands-vip-course'],
  ['Georgia Tech. “The Kendeda Building: Living Building Challenge.”', 'https://livingbuilding.gatech.edu/living-building-challenge'],
  ['Georgia Tech Strategic Plan. “Lead by Example.”', 'https://strategicplan.gatech.edu/focus/lead'],
  ['The Kendeda Building. “Solar: The Last Step For Net-Positive Energy at The Kendeda Building.” YouTube.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W134QA1mFpY'],
];
---

<Layout title="Resources">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Resources</span>
      <h1>Small actions, campus tools, and where to learn more.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Not ready to join something yet? These everyday habits and campus services still cut energy use, and they keep
        you connected to what’s next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Everyday energy actions</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>In your room</h3>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Plug chargers and monitors into a power strip and switch it off when you leave.</li>
            <li>Keep windows shut while heat or AC is running.</li>
            <li>Use your laptop’s sleep and battery-saver settings.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>In labs and classrooms</h3>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Turn off lights and equipment when you’re the last one out.</li>
            <li>Ask your lab about the Office of Sustainability’s <a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/">Sustainable Lab Certification</a>.</li>
            <li>Report rooms that are always too hot or too cold. Wasted HVAC is wasted energy.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Getting around</h3>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Ride the free <a href="https://pts.gatech.edu/stinger-bus-routes">Stinger buses</a>. Live tracking is at bus.gatech.edu.</li>
            <li>Register your bike and use the secure bike rooms. See <a href="https://www.pts.gatech.edu/commute/commute-options/bicycling-pmds/">PTS Bicycling</a>.</li>
            <li>Use <a href="https://www.pts.gatech.edu/commute/sustainable-initiatives/">MARTA discounts, carpool permits, and 40+ EV chargers</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Stay in the loop</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/">Office of Sustainability</a>. Instagram: @SustainAtGatech. Email: <a href="mailto:sustain@gatech.edu">sustain@gatech.edu</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://energyclub.gatech.edu/">Energy Club</a>: mailing list, events, and Instagram @gt_energyclub</li>
          <li><a href="https://energy.gatech.edu/education/gt-students">Strategic Energy Institute</a>: “Connections” jobs and events newsletter</li>
          <li><a href="https://livingbuilding.gatech.edu/visit/tours">Kendeda Building</a>: tours and live building performance</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Read the plans</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/2024/04/05/climate-action-plan-provides-road-map-to-net-zero-emissions/">Georgia Tech Climate Action Plan</a>: the road map to net-zero by 2050</li>
          <li><a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/sustainability-next-plan/">Sustainability Next</a>: the Institute’s sustainability strategy</li>
          <li><a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/files/2026/02/Georgia-Tech-2025-Annual-Utility-Report-Final-1.pdf">FY2025 Annual Utility Report</a>: campus energy data</li>
          <li><a href="https://sdgs.un.org/goals/goal7">UN SDG 7</a>: the global targets for clean energy</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ol class="sources">
        {
          sources.map(([text, url]) => (
            <li>
              {text} <a href={url}>{url}</a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .card .checklist li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sources {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sources li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .sources a {
    word-break: break-all;
  }
</style>
